+- `inert` is honoured by its presence on the element or an ancestor element (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18): `Node::is_focussable` also reads false for an inert node through the crate-private `Node::is_inert`, an ancestor walk, so the cached `ElementData::is_focussable` stays per element and no mutator hook is added, and the Tab walk `focus_next_node` / `focus_prev_node`, autofocus (`process_added_subtree`) and `DioxusDocument::unkeyed_actionable` skip it; `hit_inner` answers no hit at an element carrying `inert`, before any other test, so a hit passes through it; the accessibility builder's `is_hidden_from_accessibility_tree` reads true for it, so the subtree leaves the tree and the snapshot (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:558-575; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/node.rs:1424-1433; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:256; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:260-273; tests/blitz-tests/tests/inert_subtree.rs:68-194). A known limit: HTML's focus fixup is not built — a node that holds focus when it becomes inert keeps it until focus moves (pinned by `inert_subtree::removing_inert_restores_focus_hit_and_tree`), its fix owned by a `.andromeda/residuals.md` line (target: next).
+- Focus keeps `:focus-within` on its ancestors and asks for a frame: `BaseDocument::set_focus_to` returns `false` for a node not in the document, before its `Focussed node` INFO line (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1866-1869), moves `FOCUS_WITHIN` from the old focus's element ancestors to the new focus's, the shared prefix keeping it (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1890-1908), and requests a redraw (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1911-1915); `clear_focus` removes `FOCUS_WITHIN` from the cleared node's element ancestors and requests a redraw (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1846-1850; packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1852); a removed focus clears its chain (packages/blitz-dom/src/document.rs:1025-1039); `DocumentMutator::add_children_to_parent` carries the state with a moved subtree that holds the focus, or only clears the old chain when the focus left with it (packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:751-756; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:764-768; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:827-853). The `FOCUS_WITHIN` writes go through `snapshot_node_and` and mark no changed-set entry, so a focus move still marks exactly the node that lost focus and the node that gained it — as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-19-upstream-sync-visual-lint-and-real-app-readiness/report.md
+- A `select`'s choice is held as its options' `CHECKED` element state, so `:checked` matches the chosen option; an option created with a `selected` attribute is seeded `CHECKED` (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/element.rs:455-461). The rules, in the crate-private `node/select.rs` cited to the WHATWG `select` element: a select's options are its `option` children in tree order (an `optgroup`'s are not listed); an option's label is its non-empty `label` attribute, else its stripped and collapsed text, and its value its `value` attribute when present, else the text; a single-choice select is settled by HTML's selectedness setting algorithm — the last chosen option, else the first option not disabled (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/select.rs:70-86; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/select.rs:117-139; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/select.rs:155-164). The mutator records every select whose children an entry point touches and every select entering the document — a Dioxus static template is deep-cloned, so its options never pass an append —; a `selected` write sets that option chosen and its select's other options not, a cleared one sets it not chosen, and `flush` settles every recorded select, firing no event (packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1017-1020; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1097-1101; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1211-1215; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1220-1241). Dioxus writes a dynamic `selected` again on each re-render, so a controlled app writes `selected` from its `input` event's value or a choice reverts (as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-20-select-by-id/report.md). Form submission sends every chosen option that is not disabled, by its value (packages/blitz-dom/src/form.rs:276-290). The accessibility builder keeps an option whose parent is a `select` although it computes `display: none` — `hidden`, `inert` and `visibility: hidden` still exclude it —, writes its `selected` from its chosen state with no `aria-selected` read, and takes its non-empty `label` attribute as its `label` where it has no `aria-label` (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:157-162; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:171-181; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:257-258; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:260-273). The user-agent stylesheet gives `select` the border, padding and background of `input, textarea` and `display: inline-block`, and shows a single-choice select's chosen option by `select:not([multiple]) > option:checked { display: inline; }` beside `option { display: none; }`, so a select lays out as a box holding its chosen option (packages/blitz-dom/assets/default.css:77-78; packages/blitz-dom/assets/default.css:84-86; packages/blitz-dom/assets/default.css:155-159). Its keys and its click are [Scrolling and input]'s.
